        <headline>SYSTEMS BLEED AND PRESSURISATION DAILY REVIEW</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: ACMS REVIEW SHOWS RH BLEED TRIP DURING DESCENT (2 PSI). 
PREVIOUS HISTORY OF RH BLEED TRIP WITH MW0311 HARNESS AND BAR REPLACED IN LAST 3 MONTHS
HEALTH CHECK REQUIRED.

ACTION:  
1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08 ) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.
    
* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM  
    
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.
    
3. LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:     
A) PRSOV DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE     
B) SENSE LINES BETWEEN BAR AND PCCV     
C) SUPPLY SENSE LINE TO HSR     
D) SENSE LINE TO PRSOV     
E) SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR     
F) 390 SENSOR SENSE LINES FROM PCCV UNION     
G) SENSE TUBE BETWEEN HSV AND HSR

4. INSPECT THE #2 PCCV KISS SEAL IAW AMM 36-12-02. REPLACE IF NECESSARY

5. INSPECT INSTALLATION OF THE TUBES P/N 332A2350-12 AND 332A2350-14 AND ENSURE ENSURING NO PRELOAD EXISTS ON THE TUBES, BLEED AIR REGULATOR, PRECOOLER CONTROL VALVE AND CTAI DUCT.
 
6. DUE HISTORY, IF NFF REPLACE THE FOLLOWING COMPONENTS:
	6(A). PCCV IAW AMM 36-12-02/401 - LATEST REV
	6(B). 490 SENSOR IAW AMM 36-11-08/401 - LATEST REV
	6(C). 390 SENSOR IAW AMM 36-12-03/401 - LATEST REV

7. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE.

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.  

**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
